 This subject probably has been recently discussed here but since 
I think here is a major disadvantage to the player I think the dev 
team should fix it. It is about monsters who follow you up/down 
the stairs and monsters who throw things.  
 This happened to me a while ago: I was attacked by a group of elf 
zombies. I was already badly wounded so I decided to run. I was a 
valkyrie and 8th level or so, so I was fast. I knew where the stairs 
leading up were so I headed towards them. I quickly gained some 
distance to the pursuing monsters but the worst was yet to come.  
There was one of these zombies in the same room where the stairs were. 
Well, I got to the stairs and climbed up and this dummy followed me. 
When I got the level above me, all I could do was watch this zombie 
kill me. It got the first swing even though it was a slow monster and 
I was fast! If this isn't unfair then what is? 
 The same goes for monsters who throw weapons at you. They can move,  
pick up a dart (for example) and throw it at you in the same round! 
This oughta be fixed, too! 
  
  
  
 One question: if I accidentally destroy my Excalibur (by enchanting 
it too much, for instance), is it possible to achieve a new one? 
 
 PS. There's one silly thing about military barracks; whenever you are 
stealthy, the soldiers sleep. I think in every barrack there should be 
at least one guard who cried alert if the player enters the room the 
soldiers are in. Sleeping soldiers are too easy to kill.  
